Going around as a Xorn is very risky, as you so painfully learned.
They have few HP, and they need a cornuthaum for MC and an artifact for
MR. Without magic cancellation and magic resistance, you can be screwed
very badly. Also, it is very bad in Slashem to 'depolymorph' due to
hitpoint loss, especially when you have polymorph control. (You lose a
LOT of MAX HP).

The safest way to face the Master Assassin is NOT to polymorph into a
Xorn. Instead, you can stay on the upstairs, burn an Elbereth, and wake
him remotely with a powerful pet or something like a drum of
earthquake.  If you do decide to polymorph into a Xorn to get inside
his chamber, remember:
1) Use ESP to make sure that you are not emerging into a herd of Nagas
2) Use Elbereth to keep the Nagas from attacking
3) Once you are inside the chamber, you can polymorph again, into a
crystal golem.  That will give you 300 HP, plus magic resistance and
level-drain resistance.

Although the Master Key is a really nice artifact, providing teleport
control and half physical damage, you probably don't REALLY need it
before the castle - especially since the Hand of Vecna will also give
you 1/2 damage

